  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Tim Drygala is a German legal scholar and professor at the University of Leipzig, specialising in civil, commercial and company law. Trained in Giessen and Bonn, he joined Leipzig after research at Harvard Law School and visiting teaching appointments. His academic work includes creditor protection and the regulation of securities terms.",
    "html": "<p>Tim Drygala is a German legal scholar and professor at the University of Leipzig, specialising in civil, commercial and company law. Trained in Giessen and Bonn, he joined Leipzig after research at Harvard Law School and visiting teaching appointments. His academic work includes creditor protection and the regulation of securities terms.</p>\r\n",
    "word_count": 51,
