  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "As dean of Leipzig's law faculty, Tim Drygala faced the practical demands of expanding student numbers. He advocated stronger support at the start of the degree, better exam preparation and a revised curriculum. He also pressed for new premises because the existing accommodation could not meet the enlarged faculty's needs.\n\nHis approach to the role emphasised bringing colleagues together and advancing their ideas, rather than treating the dean as a corporate chief executive. Alongside that administrative work, he researched how digital processes could make it easier and faster to establish companies.",
    "html": "<p>As dean of Leipzig's law faculty, Tim Drygala faced the practical demands of expanding student numbers. He advocated stronger support at the start of the degree, better exam preparation and a revised curriculum. He also pressed for new premises because the existing accommodation could not meet the enlarged faculty's needs.</p>\r\n<p>His approach to the role emphasised bringing colleagues together and advancing their ideas, rather than treating the dean as a corporate chief executive. Alongside that administrative work, he researched how digital processes could make it easier and faster to establish companies.</p>\r\n",
